r.save('Persist seven individually reasoned authorization/order record contexts, then union-selected remaining delivery/service/query functions.')
contexts={
'src/Falah.Domain/Authorization/Actor.cs':'Sealed positional Actor record carries Id,Name,Role,Active and IReadOnlySet Permissions. Generated init/with-copy is shallow for permission-set reference; equality uses collection reference, not deep permission equivalence. A trusted caller can retain and mutate concrete HashSet even though property interface is read-only; no external API alias path proven. Record Role alone grants nothing; real policy uses Active and permissions. No database/user lookup or authentication is synthesized.',
'src/Falah.Domain/Authorization/ManagerApproval.cs':'Sealed positional ManagerApproval record stores seven presentation fields including registry ID, claimed approver identity/role/time/action/reason. Public generated constructor/with-copy can freely construct those claims, but registry lookup/action/single-use validation supplies actual authority. Equality is all presentation components, not validity or consumption. Generated ToString can expose approval ID if caller logs object, no actual logging path established. FIN017 family demonstrates why unvalidated presentation name must not be treated as proof.',
'src/Falah.Domain/Authorization/PinHasher.cs':'Sealed positional HashedPin record contains Base64 hash/salt and iteration count. Generated constructor/with-copy does not validate encodings, length or positive iteration count; actual hashing creates correct values, verification can throw on malformed metadata. Equality compares exact Base64 strings and count, not whether two salted hashes authenticate same PIN. Generated printing could include hash/salt fields; no clear PIN field or proven log leak, and no secret data copied into audit.',
'src/Falah.Domain/Authorization/PermissionCatalog.cs':'Sealed positional PermissionDefinition record has Key and Category string components. Generated equality/copy/deconstruction compares both strings, whereas operational catalog Keys discards Category for permission membership. Two definitions same Key different Category are unequal records but represent same capability key; no automatic duplicate-key prevention or policy authority. Catalog contents manually checked separately, not inferred from generated equality.',
'src/Falah.Domain/Orders/OrderItem.cs':'Sealed positional OrderItem record captures14 identity/product/variant/name/price/quantity/total/routing/rule/note components. Generated construction and with-copy do not enforce TotalPrice=UnitPrice*Quantity, quantity positive or station allowed. Server MenuPricing builds authoritative snapshot but unchecked multiplication remains FIN016 extension. Immutable strings/Money/scalars copy by value/reference safely; record cannot query current menu, so later product edits do not automatically alter historical snapshot. Value equality all fields is not order-line DB identity.',
'src/Falah.Domain/Orders/OrderRefund.cs':'Sealed positional OrderRefund record stores request/operation/key/amount/channel/movement/time/actor/approver/reason/original and operational shifts. Generated constructor/with-copy does not enforce positive amount, paid entitlement, refund aggregate cap or real approval/movement existence. Order.ApplyRefund enforces amount cap, handler owns financial checks, and FIN003/004 remain cross-file workflow defects. Equality includes all components, not just refundId; no ledger or treasury write synthesized.',
'src/Falah.Domain/Orders/ElectronicPayment.cs':'Sealed positional ElectronicPayment record has Method, optionalProvider, Amount and Status, supporting value equality/copy/deconstruction. Generated with-copy can change status to Confirmed but does not post treasury, consume journal or freeze/unfreeze dispatch; Confirm handler is responsible. Single object represents only one electronic leg, not multiple independent pending channels. Source comment promises pending operational freeze, but readiness/assignment code does not universally enforce it; preserve as qualified workflow evidence, not constructor vulnerability.'}
for path,reason in contexts.items():
 source=json.loads((k.WORK/'Knowledge/Source-Symbols-CallableFacets/Files'/(path+'.json')).read_text(encoding='utf8'));assert len(source['generated_behavior_inputs'])==1
